Think of it as an ingredients list for software.

Example:

Docker Image
     │
     ▼
SBOM
     │
     ├── Python 3.12
     ├── Flask
     ├── Werkzeug
     ├── Jinja2
     ├── Linux packages
     └── Other dependencies

Syft generates this inventory.

Example flow:

Docker Image
     │
     ▼
Syft
     │
     ▼
SBOM
     │
     ├── Package name
     ├── Version
     ├── License
     └── Dependency information

Why this is important:

Imagine six months later:

Critical vulnerability discovered
          │
          ▼
Which applications contain this package?
          │
          ▼
SBOM tells us

