Option 1: Ignore a specific line (Best Practice)

API_KEY = "dummy-test-value"  # gitleaks:allow - Gitleaks will ignore that line only.



Option 2: Baseline File (Enterprise Approach)

Generate a baseline:

gitleaks detect \
  --no-git \
  --source . \
  --report-format json \
  --report-path baseline.json

Then:

gitleaks detect \
  --no-git \
  --source . \
  --baseline-path baseline.json

Now findings already present in the baseline are ignored.

This is common when onboarding Gitleaks to an existing large codebase.



