Step 1 — Scale the bad ReplicaSet to zero

First see the ReplicaSets:

kubectl get rs -n dev

The bad Pods all belong to:

myapp-my-app-chart-5d97c8b6dc

Scale that ReplicaSet to zero:

kubectl scale rs myapp-my-app-chart-5d97c8b6dc -n dev --replicas=0
Step 2 — Delete all Pods from the bad ReplicaSet using the pod-template hash

Your bad Pods have:

pod-template-hash=5d97c8b6dc

Delete them all in one command:

kubectl delete pods -n dev \
  -l pod-template-hash=5d97c8b6dc \
  --force --grace-period=0

This is the safest approach because it targets only the broken AppArmor ReplicaSet.

Your healthy Pod:

myapp-my-app-chart-5f8fdf8649-pj8r7   1/1 Running

has a different ReplicaSet hash and will not be selected.

